{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1793 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "76ccc223559338fdd6f47a49219199e21b1baab249ca3d1c7342b76fbf8b868b" :edb/db-before-t 1792 :edb/db-after-t 1793 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535105 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:58:24.078Z" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087491 1100 "Given that the asymptotes of the hyperbola below are $y=\\pm\\dfrac{5}{7}x$, find the parametric equations of the hyperbola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/873/Source/Images/6dac6525092db5cbe84cc8ace803557c.png)" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087491 1100 "Given that the asymptotes of the hyperbola below are $y=\\pm\\dfrac{5}{7}x,$ find the parametric equations of the hyperbola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/fd2618e961c15a9b0665e73e18544ab08b0d611b962bc3771558c61450cf49e5.png)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087491 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\sec{t},\\quad y=b\\tan{t}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a, 0)$. From the graph, we have that $(7,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=7$.\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x\n$$\n\nIn our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm\\dfrac57x\n$$\n\nand so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{b}{a} &= \\frac{5}{7} \\\\\n\\frac{b}{7} &= \\frac{5}{7} \\\\\nb &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=7\\sec{t},\\quad y=5\\tan{t}\n$$" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087491 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\sec{t},\\quad y=b\\tan{t},\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a, 0).$ From the graph, we have that $(7,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=7.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm\\dfrac57x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ \\frac{b}{7} & =\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=7\\sec{t},\\quad y=5\\tan{t}.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087492 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola with the parametric equations $x = 6\\sec{t},\\, y = 4 \\sqrt{2}\\tan{t}$." 13194139535105 false] [17592186087492 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola with the parametric equations $x = 6\\sec{t},\\, y = 4 \\sqrt{2}\\tan{t}.$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087492 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t$. We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\sec t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= 6\\sec t \\\\\n\\frac{x}{6} &= \\sec t \\\\\n(\\frac{x}{6})^{2} &= (\\sec t)^{2} \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{6^{2}} &= \\sec^{2} t \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{36} &= \\sec^{2} t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\tan{t}$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= 4\\sqrt{2}\\tan t \\\\\n\\frac{y}{4\\sqrt{2}} &= \\tan t \\\\\n(\\frac{y}{4\\sqrt{2}})^{2} &= (\\tan t)^{2} \\\\\n(y^{2})/((4\\sqrt{2})^{2}) &= \\tan^{2} t \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{32} &= \\tan^{2} t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity\n\n$$\n\\tan^2{t} + 1 = \\sec^2{t}\n$$\n\nand rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan^{2} t + 1 &= \\sec^{2} t \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{32} + 1 &= \\frac{x^{2}}{36} \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{36} - \\frac{y^{2}}{32} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087492 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\sec t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{6} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ {(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2} & ={(\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\tan{t}$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{4\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {(\\frac{y}{4\\sqrt{2}})}^{2} & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(4\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{32} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity $\\tan^2{t} + 1 = \\sec^2{t}$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{32}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{32} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087580 1100 "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\displaystyle\\frac{x^2}{49} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1$?" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087580 1100 "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\displaystyle\\frac{x^2}{49} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1?$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087580 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\sec{t},\\quad y=b\\tan{t}\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{49} = 7\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nb =\\sqrt9= 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=7\\sec{t},\\quad y=3\\tan{t}\n$$" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087580 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\sec{t},\\quad y=b\\tan{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a = \\sqrt{49} = 7$ and $b =\\sqrt9= 3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=7\\sec{t},\\quad y=3\\tan{t}.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087581 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/6e12d114aedfd6c5c8ab5830e052fcc1dd3c937b825665a0490b42ca0c87972c.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx = \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\qquad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087581 1100 "The quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/873/Source/Images/c60e96f8795a9be0304c10941f61c928.png)\n\n$x = \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\qquad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}$.\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t$?" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087581 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2 \\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3 \\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in [-\\pi,\\pi], \\quad\nt \\neq \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}2.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/730325137cfca58eb17d65103e539d084f81d7ab810628261125c29dbb8a0284.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $\\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right)$ we get the required quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right).\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186087581 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2 \\sec{t}, \\quad y = \\sqrt3 \\tan{t}, \\quad t \\in [-\\pi,\\pi], \\quad t \\neq \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}2\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/873/Source/Images/446c464de9a66d886281a25f332bc654.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $[MATH: \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right)]$ we get the required quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$[MATH: x= \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\quad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}, \\quad t \\in \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right).]$" 13194139535105 false] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331422 13194139535105 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331427 13194139535105 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331443 13194139535105 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331449 13194139535105 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331454 13194139535105 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331394 13194139535105 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331401 13194139535105 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331408 13194139535105 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331459 13194139535105 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331490 13194139535105 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331433 13194139535105 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331437 13194139535105 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331440 13194139535105 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331476 13194139535105 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331483 13194139535105 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331415 13194139535105 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331463 13194139535105 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331470 13194139535105 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331497 13194139535105 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331504 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331395 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1089 "q-106522" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1113 #uuid "ad96cb18-bd6b-5a64-9cd7-5ecc565723d2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331394 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{4} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331396 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331397 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331398 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331399 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331400 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1041 "selection" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331399 13194139535105 true] [17592186331395 1110 #uuid "560064db-80ec-5712-b706-53edcb4fdb4a" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331396 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331396 1111 #uuid "b45ea980-dd72-50a4-9c54-757af2cbc3eb" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331397 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331397 1111 #uuid "37338cf5-43ef-5a88-9aaa-ef87b102e514" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331398 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331398 1111 #uuid "a3eda697-bd17-509e-a542-897de33720bb" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331399 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331399 1111 #uuid "dc0bab88-fbaa-5b0c-ab00-ae659f5ba695" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331400 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331400 1111 #uuid "400c700e-61ee-5fd9-8dcd-94bbe6c6dff7" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331402 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1089 "q-106527" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1113 #uuid "9c1e05d1-cdc3-5f99-b424-96705dd43abe" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331401 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331403 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331404 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331405 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331406 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331407 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1041 "selection" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331404 13194139535105 true] [17592186331402 1110 #uuid "bc4ac55b-74bb-5316-90a4-762217d978c1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331403 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331403 1111 #uuid "a7420e16-5924-53f3-b61c-97b9fa39437f" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331404 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331404 1111 #uuid "33639763-4461-572a-9af6-cdc1c81a16f4" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331405 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331405 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331405 1111 #uuid "a375ba33-56ae-5c6a-a380-792e5d9307e0" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331406 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331406 1111 #uuid "a59e4288-447a-5b62-8bad-e3c7b88f126f" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331407 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331407 1111 #uuid "53348bd7-b394-5515-8130-6324c1c9ac6c" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331409 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1089 "q-106528" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1113 #uuid "f30b1e07-07d4-58c1-a237-16af51b64840" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331408 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(5)^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331410 13194139535105 true] [17592186331409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331411 13194139535105 true] [17592186331409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331412 13194139535105 true] [17592186331409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331413 13194139535105 