\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331415 1113 #uuid "00f90cad-f323-5203-8ecf-124e55c6a024" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331415 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/d8f735790daf267a094ecd8c336d90de65d84e3985485213eb541364bd14aacd.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ we get only the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331417 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331418 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331419 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331420 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331421 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1041 "selection" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331421 13194139535105 true] [17592186331416 1110 #uuid "46c567a0-a6f7-5dde-b7fa-9a31eb2791a2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331417 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331417 1111 #uuid "deb32eb7-6f5b-5ebc-8b65-ceac2de901a7" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331418 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331418 1111 #uuid "8b7db0c5-d87c-5d5d