, so $a=2.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{b}{2} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331424 13194139535105 true] [17592186331423 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331423 1041 "field-1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331423 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331424 13194139535105 true] [17592186331423 1110 #uuid "d6875cb5-cc3c-5f78-88bf-d097db699f0e" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331424 1034 "2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331424 1111 #uuid "df4c4eb8-96a0-545d-a6f8-499124fc191e" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331425 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331426 13194139535105 true] [17592186331425 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331425 1041 "field-2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331425 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331426 13194139535105 true] [17592186331425 1110 #uuid "9f077401-361a-57c7-a4a2-8417e7e4c1f0" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331426 1034 "5\\tan(t)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331426 1111 #uuid "ec90d138-f991-5591-a271-d92e9a9b83bb" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331428 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331431 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1089 "q-274725" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/f81019b6a22b93d480be339eb2b58c642a2a01a098d0a74eb172c873ca254b09.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1113 #uuid "24d693f3-c81f-529f-ae93-8dafeedac4b2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331427 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{5},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ b & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331429 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331430 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1041 "field-1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331430 13194139535105 true] [17592186331428 1110 #uuid "3690e7d4-c802-5423-adbb-c82a4e70da0a" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331429 1034 "5\\sec(t)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331429 1111 #uuid "e1d55664-2fec-560d-86a0-d2ffb3f8e6fb" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331430 1034 "\\sqrt{5}\\sec(t)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [