tered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(3,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{b}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331450 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331451 13194139535105 true] [17592186331450 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331450 1041 "field-1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331450 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331451 13194139535105 true] [17592186331450 1110 #uuid "6d173244-2112-5a3d-9f87-a2db1e24abff" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331451 1034 "3" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331451 1111 #uuid "632913a9-9187-5044-8d6c-729a81a5b2ef" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331452 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331452 1041 "field-2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331452 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331452 1110 #uuid "98d90fa3-d556-5625-bfff-78d2a16e0840" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331453 1034 "\\sqrt{7}\\tan(t)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331453 1111 #uuid "e5e49199-0569-530d-8d96-4347ddf0e98c" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331455 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331457 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1089 "q-325927" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/6a4ee1fd218118096dcdb2bd85b16477e2230b4634eb6c53e9fcab68f7d4939c.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1113 #uuid "9a90e399-12c3-5736-af8a-cd387ebebbf8" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331454 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{6},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{6}} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331455 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331456 13194139535105 true] [17592186331455 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331455 1041 "field-1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331455 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331456 13194139535105 true] [17592186331455 1110 #uuid "759de39f-b2cd-59e7-af40-484bd1d8006d" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331456 1034 "\\sqrt{6}\\sec(t)" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331456 1111 #uuid "9628d248-208e-56c9-944f-e9eac8f9c3b1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331458 13194139535105 true] [17592186331457 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331457 1041 "field-2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331457 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331458 13194139535105 true] [17592186331457 1110 #uuid "5f88f637-a2e4-5bdc-9efe-f14f5d46151e" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331458 1034 "2" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331458 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331458 1111 #uuid "f5ac3534-c327-5568-b66f-a3a33718964d" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331460 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1089 "q-325936" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1113 #uuid "54771605-b35b-5b36-a1fc-58560ab4c2be" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331459 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{8}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331461 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331462 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1041 "field-1" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331462 13194139535105 true] [17592186331460 1110 #uuid "cd1c043d-3a53-5737-ac6d-684eabdef5a0" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331461 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{8}" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331461 1111 #uuid "b9ab8ae3-9848-5917-8d28-d29830e6a2f9" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331462 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{25}-\\frac{y^2}{8}" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535105 true] [17592186331462 1111 #uuid "70797d34-ae52-5261-93b8-79b4498cae51" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331464 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331466 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331468 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1089 "q-325980" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/7db943c53e70d9b77490c2d73acac939be08fdfa4b0aa958addb2d50b6078543.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$\n\n$t\\in [$\n$-\\pi ,$\n{{field-1}}$)⋃($\n{{field-2}}\n$,$\n{{field-3}}$]$" 13194139535105 true] [17592186331463 1113 #uuid "69e36e58-af14-55f7-8286-96236a606bc1" 13194139535105 true] [17